 b:"Daratumumab had given rapid, deep responses in relapsed AL amyloidosis, and VCd was the most widely used frontline regimen.",
 i:"The first approved therapy for AL amyloidosis and the current standard first-line treatment; the final analysis showed that deeper hematologic response translated into longer survival.",
 q:"Stage IIIb patients, those at greatest risk, were excluded; whether transplantation adds to daratumumab-VCd, and how long to continue daratumumab, are untested.",
 cm:[[34345020,"Onuora S, Nat Rev Rheumatol 2021","New treatments for amyloidosis"],[42658522,"Chakraborty R, Blood 2026","Daratumumab in AL amyloidosis: survival, cardiac CR, and beyond"]],
